The change from `TransportVersion` to `CompatibilityVersions` is consistent across these diffs, but there are a few areas where the logic could be improved for clarity and correctness.
In `#D1FZH`, the logger message in `NodeTransportVersionTask.onFailure` should reflect the new type:
```java
logger.error("Could not apply compatibility versions for nodes {} to cluster state", results.keySet(), e);
```
This is already addressed in your changes, but ensure that all similar messages are updated accordingly.
In `#PC1GK`, the logic around checking and updating `systemIndexMappingsVersion` could be clearer:
```java
var systemIndexMappingsVersion = Optional.ofNullable(currentCompatibilityVersions)
    .map(CompatibilityVersions::systemIndexMappingsVersion)
    .orElse(Map.of());
if (Objects.equals(recordedTv, INFERRED_TRANSPORT_VERSION) || systemIndexMappingsVersion.isEmpty()) {
    builder.putCompatibilityVersions(
        e.getKey(),
        e.getValue().transportVersion(),
        e.getValue().systemIndexMappingsVersion()
    );
    modified = true;
}
```
This logic is correct but could be simplified by directly using `currentCompatibilityVersions`:
```java
if (Objects.equals(recordedTv, INFERRED_TRANSPORT_VERSION) || 
    currentCompatibilityVersions == null || 
    currentCompatibilityVersions.systemIndexMappingsVersion().isEmpty()) {
    builder.putCompatibilityVersions(
        e.getKey(),
        e.getValue().transportVersion(),
        e.getValue().systemIndexMappingsVersion()
    );
    modified = true;
}
```
In `#Y4741`, the transformation from `NodeInfo` to `CompatibilityVersions` is correct, but ensure that `n.getCompatibilityVersions()` returns a non-null value:
```java
Map<String, CompatibilityVersions> results = response.getNodes()
    .stream()
    .collect(
        Collectors.toUnmodifiableMap(
            n -> n.getNode().getId(),
            n -> new CompatibilityVersions(n.getTransportVersion(), n.getCompatibilityVersions())
        )
    );
```
If `n.getCompatibilityVersions()` can be null, handle it appropriately:
```java
Map<String, CompatibilityVersions> results = response.getNodes()
    .stream()
    .collect(
        Collectors.toUnmodifiableMap(
            n -> n.getNode().getId(),
            n -> new CompatibilityVersions(n.getTransportVersion(), Optional.ofNullable(n.getCompatibilityVersions()).orElse(Map.of()))
        )
    );
```

